Like Cui Kaiyi said,

573
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:54,400
feelings

574
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:55,960
come first.

575
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:56,840
Exactly.

576
00:22:56,840 --> 00:22:58,920
If things don't work out in real life,

577
00:22:58,920 --> 00:23:00,320
those feelings can fade pretty quickly.

578
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:01,360
That actually reflects

579
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:02,320
how she's feeling

580
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:03,480
right now.

581
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,880
Sha Yue'er is starting to hesitate too.

582
00:23:05,440 --> 00:23:06,400
She's hesitating too.

583
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:07,840
I can understand

584
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:09,360
why she only half believes him.

585
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:10,560
I think what she really wants

586
00:23:10,560 --> 00:23:11,280
in a relationship

587
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:12,240
is someone who will choose her

588
00:23:12,240 --> 00:23:13,320
above everyone else,

589
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:14,160
and make her the only person

590
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:15,280
they truly favor.

591
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:16,880
I feel like Sha Yue'er

592
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:17,800
is at a point

593
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:18,920
where she's being

594
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,080
pretty honest with herself

595
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:21,080
about how she feels.

596
00:23:21,080 --> 00:23:21,800
She doesn't need

597
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:23,080
to rush

598
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,360
into making a decision

599
00:23:24,360 --> 00:23:25,600
or forcing herself to do anything.

600
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:26,480
So I actually think

601
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:28,200
she really values herself

602
00:23:28,200 --> 00:23:29,840
and this relationship.

603
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,160
That's why

604
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:32,320
she has so much on her mind right now.

605
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:34,480
This is something
she needs to work through.

606
00:23:34,480 --> 00:23:35,520
All of her inner needs

607
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:36,640
are being projected onto two people.

608
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,560
Zhao Xilun

609
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:38,280
and Chen Hewen.

610
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:39,960
So, Dai Xu, which one would you choose?

611
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:43,320
I'd probably lean toward Zhao Xilun.

612
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:44,360
(Cupid Dai Xu)
I think a girl

613
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,680
should definitely find a guy

614
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,440
who treats her well.

615
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:48,720
Then I'd choose Chen Hewen.

616
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:50,120
Because I think

617
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:51,200
that instant attraction

618
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:51,960
is really important.

619
00:23:51,960 --> 00:23:53,200
I feel like in this world,

620
00:23:53,200 --> 00:23:55,160
it's rare to really like someone.

621
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:56,400
I just want to be with someone I like.

622
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,520
I don't need anything else.

623
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:58,960
I can take care of myself.

624
00:24:09,380 --> 00:24:10,420
(Yu Yang returns to Signal House)

625
00:24:10,440 --> 00:24:11,200
Yu Yang is back.

626
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:16,800
He's looking even better now.

627
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:19,360
Once you meet someone you like,

628
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:21,680
(Looking around)
you start caring more about your looks.

629
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:22,520
Yeah.

630
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:26,440
Hello.

631
00:24:27,080 --> 00:24:27,880
You're back.

632
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:29,840
I was the first one back.

633
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:32,880
I didn't see anyone.

634
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,560
Why hasn't she (Liang Renfang)
come back yet?

635
00:24:39,140 --> 00:24:41,660
(Pinching)

636
00:24:42,900 --> 00:24:44,660
(Checking the time)

637
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:50,040
They're waiting for their girls.

638
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:55,840
(Cao Yiheng)
I'm getting pretty sleepy.

639
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:57,400
I came back before sunset.

640
00:24:57,920 --> 00:24:59,080
So you've been here for hours.

641
00:24:59,880 --> 00:25:00,600
You're the only one here?

642
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:03,520
Zhao Xilun

643
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:04,920
went to the stargazing room.

644
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:06,800
He was the second one back.

645
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:07,960
He went to the stargazing room.

646
00:25:10,480 --> 00:25:12,040
Let's wait a little longer.

647
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:13,600
Come on, Yu Yang.

648
00:25:13,600 --> 00:25:14,760
Let's go downstairs and walk around.

649
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:15,380
Let's go.

650
00:25:15,380 --> 00:25:16,140
They can't sit still anymore.

651
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,560
It's so quiet today.

652
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:19,560
Yeah.

653
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,000
Nobody's back.

654
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,160
He starts

655
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:24,840
rock climbing.

656
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:26,920
Time flies when you're doing something.

657
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:30,700
(Suddenly appears)

658
00:25:30,720 --> 00:25:31,800
So cute.

659
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:38,200
Careful.

660
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:39,440
Be careful.

661
00:25:49,040 --> 00:25:49,880
It feels so good

662
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:50,480
when you jump down.

663
00:25:52,320 --> 00:25:54,160
(Fixing his hair)
Why aren't they back yet?

664
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,240
I don't know.

665
00:25:55,560 --> 00:25:57,560
I really like my hair like this.

666
00:25:58,360 --> 00:25:59,560
But I really want to jump down

667
00:25:59,840 --> 00:26:00,640
and just fly over there.

668
00:26:04,640 --> 00:26:05,280
That feels so good.

669
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:06,960
He doesn't know what to do anymore.

670
00:26:07,640 --> 00:26:08,560
He's not used to

671
00:26:08,560 --> 00:26:09,480
being on his own.

672
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:10,680
(Having a hard time being alone)

673
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:11,720
He's not used to being alone.

674
00:26:11,720 --> 00:26:12,360
He's not used to

675
00:26:12,360 --> 00:26:13,640
being on his own.

676
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:17,580
(Pretending to shoot a basketball)

677
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:19,320
What time is it already?

678
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:20,080
Why aren't they back yet?

679
00:26:20,800 --> 00:26:22,240
They're not coming back.
They all went on dates.

680
00:26:24,400 --> 00:26:25,160
Let's play badminton.

681
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:26,560
Sure.

682
00:26:36,820 --> 00:26:38,080
(Looking)
Who's back?

683
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:39,160
Who?

684
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:39,680
Chen Hewen.

685
00:26:40,700 --> 00:26:41,420
(Chen Hewen returns to Signal House)

686
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:42,080
Chen Hewen.

687
00:26:42,800 --> 00:26:44,040
Hello.

688
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:44,880
Hello.

689
00:26:45,160 --> 00:26:45,800
I got back a little late.

690
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:46,920
I got back pretty late.

691
00:26:46,920 --> 00:26:47,760
Not many people are back.

692
00:26:47,760 --> 00:26:48,680
It's just the three of us.

693
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,400
Just the three of us?

694
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:51,340
Zhao Xilun went to the stargazing room.

695
00:26:51,340 --> 00:26:52,440
Zhao Xilun is at that, uh...

696
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:53,390
Oh my God.

697
00:26:55,160 --> 00:26:56,440
He just found out?

698
00:26:57,080 --> 00:26:57,880
He only just found out.

699
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,650
I'm gonna go put my stuff away first.

700
00:27:01,650 --> 00:27:02,520
Go ahead.

701
00:27:03,860 --> 00:27:06,220
(Jogs)

702
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:19,640
Feels like we haven't met in ages.

703
00:27:19,640 --> 00:27:20,840
It's only been a day,

704
00:27:20,840 --> 00:27:21,400
Chris.

705
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:24,000
Please pick a seat.

706
00:27:24,700 --> 00:27:26,900
(Private Romantic Dinner, Summer Breeze)

707
00:27:27,360 --> 00:27:28,200
I'll sit here.

708
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:29,480
Please.

709
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:29,920
Okay.

710
00:27:30,700 --> 00:27:31,460
(Pulls out the chair)

711
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:32,320
He's really thoughtful.

712
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:33,280
Thank you.

713
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:34,160
Chris.

714
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:34,600
You're welcome.

715
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:39,960
I'm sitting down.

716
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:40,680
Go ahead.

717
00:27:48,120 --> 00:27:48,800
Here.

718
00:27:48,820 --> 00:27:50,060
(Hands over the food)

719
00:27:50,240 --> 00:27:50,920
Thank you.

720
00:27:52,080 --> 00:27:52,960
What do we have?
I'll just grab whatever.

721
00:27:52,960 --> 00:27:55,040
(Sha Yue'er)
I think this is wagyu and pineapple.

722
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:56,360
This should be yakitori.

723
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:56,840
And this one's okra.

724
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:57,880
Let's dig in.

725
00:27:57,880 --> 00:27:58,520
You too.

726
00:27:58,520 --> 00:27:59,080
Okay.

727
00:27:59,080 --> 00:27:59,480
Go ahead.

728
00:27:59,960 --> 00:28:01,000
He's looking good.

729
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,280
I think it's what he's wearing today.

730
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:03,120
It looks good on him.

731
00:28:03,120 --> 00:28:04,520
He looks pretty classy.

732
00:28:04,520 --> 00:28:05,040
How do I put it?

733
00:28:05,040 --> 00:28:06,040
He has that youthful vibe.

734
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:08,000
Help yourself.

735
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:09,520
Looks pretty good.

736
00:28:10,280 --> 00:28:11,240
So good.

737
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:12,840
It's actually really good.

738
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:16,840
Were you busy today?

739
00:28:17,760 --> 00:28:19,200
Probably about as busy as you were.

740
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:21,000
So you were pretty busy,
but you still made time to...

741
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,440
(Hands it over)
Thanks. Yeah.

742
00:28:22,440 --> 00:28:23,920
(Zhao Xilun)
Made time to come early.

743
00:28:23,920 --> 00:28:24,560
Yeah.

744
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:25,240
That means a lot to me.

745
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:27,280
How about you?

746
00:28:29,840 --> 00:28:31,560
Let me tell you some good news.

747
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:33,200
What good news?

748
00:28:34,320 --> 00:28:35,200
Last night,

749
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:37,960
I got an interview at Imperial College.

750
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:40,680
An interview at Imperial College?

751
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:41,280
Yeah.

752
00:28:41,280 --> 00:28:42,280
That's impressive.

753
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:44,120
When's the interview?

754
00:28:44,120 --> 00:28:44,720
Tomorrow.

755
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:46,260
I was on the fence about it.

756
00:28:46,260 --> 00:28:47,340
I'll see if I can make it
through the interview.

757
00:28:47,340 --> 00:28:48,560
You definitely can.

758
00:28:48,560 --> 00:28:49,200
I hope you're right.

759
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:50,760
I just feel

760
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:51,760
really lucky today.

761
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:57,360
We have cake too.

762
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:00,120
What kind of cake?

763
00:29:00,120 --> 00:29:01,080
It's got...

764
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:02,920
I remember you like

765
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,880
lychee, cherries, and mango.

766
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:05,920
Right?

767
00:29:06,560 --> 00:29:07,520
(Nods)
He remembers everything.

768
00:29:07,520 --> 00:29:08,440
He really does.

769
00:29:11,380 --> 00:29:12,020
(Cake prepared by Zhao Xilun)

770
00:29:12,040 --> 00:29:12,800
It must be nice.

771
00:29:15,040 --> 00:29:15,640
Happy.

772
00:29:16,660 --> 00:29:18,700
(Glances)

773
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:20,000
Can I ask you something?

774
00:29:21,680 --> 00:29:22,680
What is it?

775
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,840
Are you the clingy type?

776
00:29:28,400 --> 00:29:30,120
I used to be.

777
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:31,840
But I don't know if I am anymore.

778
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:33,280
I feel like I'm going through changes.

779
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:37,080
What does "clingy" mean to you?

780
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:39,000
I don't know either.

781
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:42,840
Do you think you need

782
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:43,740
a lot of personal space?

783
00:29:43,820 --> 00:29:45,060
(Follows up)

784
00:29:45,140 --> 00:29:46,660
(Tries not to laugh)

785
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:47,840
I guess it depends on
what you mean by "a lot".

786
00:29:48,320 --> 00:29:49,440
I need some space to grow on my own

787
00:29:50,240 --> 00:29:51,720
and some personal space when I need it.

788
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:53,280
But I don't need that much space.

789
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:54,480
Yeah.

790
00:29:54,880 --> 00:29:56,520
Really? That's how you feel?

791
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:57,720
That's honestly how I feel.

792
00:29:58,160 --> 00:29:58,840
So do you think...

793
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:01,480
Am I asking too many questions?

794
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:03,160
Ask away.

795
00:30:08,120 --> 00:30:09,040
Do you think a sense of security

796
00:30:09,040 --> 00:30:09,960
comes from yourself,

797
00:30:09,960 --> 00:30:11,120
or does it come from your partner?

798
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:12,800
Sha Yue'er finally said

799
00:30:12,800 --> 00:30:13,760
what's on her mind.

800
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,280
Your partner should give you some,

801
00:30:18,280 --> 00:30:19,960
but you need to have it
within yourself first.

802
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:21,880
That makes sense.

803
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:24,960
What your partner gives you can help

804
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:25,720
keep that feeling alive.

805
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:29,920
But you have to have it

806
00:30:29,920 --> 00:30:30,800
in you first.

807
00:30:33,840 --> 00:30:35,360
Otherwise, no matter how much they give,

808
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:36,200
it won't be enough.

809
00:30:39,880 --> 00:30:40,320
I agree.

810
00:30:41,200 --> 00:30:41,880
Absolutely.

811
00:30:44,520 --> 00:30:45,380
You're pretty insightful.

812
00:30:45,620 --> 00:30:46,500
(Praise)

813
00:30:54,800 --> 00:30:56,520
Do you know when my birthday is?

814
00:30:58,640 --> 00:30:59,120
That question.

815
00:30:59,120 --> 00:30:59,960
She's comparing them.

816
00:31:02,080 --> 00:31:03,800
Do you know when my birthday is?

817
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:05,180
July 17th.

818
00:31:05,180 --> 00:31:05,900
(Blurts it out)

819
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:07,520
You've got a pretty good memory.

820
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:09,480
Zhao Xilun really remembers everything.

821
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:10,360
What?

822
00:31:10,520 --> 00:31:12,120
Nothing. It just suddenly came to mind.

823
00:31:12,920 --> 00:31:13,560
Okay.

824
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:16,040
Zhao Xilun really gets points for this.

825
00:31:16,600 --> 00:31:18,480
I am starting to see
your fearful attachment tendencies.

826
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,560
You know what fearful attachment is now?

827
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:22,240
I looked it up.

828
00:31:23,040 --> 00:31:24,680
You tend to seek reassurance
about the same things.

829
00:31:25,240 --> 00:31:25,720
Yes.

830
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:28,280
This doesn't feel like
an interrogation, does it?

831
00:31:29,700 --> 00:31:30,740
(Watches)

832
00:31:32,740 --> 00:31:34,260
(Puts down chopsticks)

833
00:31:34,880 --> 00:31:35,760
Not exactly an interrogation,

834
00:31:35,760 --> 00:31:37,520
but I can tell you are...

835
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:40,600
What?

836
00:31:43,120 --> 00:31:45,340
Perhaps you are seeking
a sense of security.

837
00:31:45,340 --> 00:31:46,660
(I can tell that you are seeking
a sense of security)

838
00:31:48,120 --> 00:31:48,880
That is exactly right.

839
00:31:52,640 --> 00:31:53,960
He can recognize

840
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:55,360
what she needs.

841
00:31:55,760 --> 00:31:56,240
Yes.

842
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,680
I think I am somewhat
afraid to be vulnerable.

843
00:32:03,820 --> 00:32:05,420
(I am afraid to be vulnerable)
Sha Yue'er is gradually opening up.

844
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:06,760
Are you afraid

845
00:32:07,200 --> 00:32:08,000
when it comes to love?

846
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,120
Yes.

847
00:32:10,960 --> 00:32:12,480
I look forward to it,
but I am afraid of it.

848
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:13,440
I want to get

849
00:32:13,440 --> 00:32:14,260
closer, but I am afraid.

850
00:32:14,340 --> 00:32:17,020
(I want to get closer, but I am afraid)

851
00:32:17,840 --> 00:32:18,960
Perhaps I also worry

852
00:32:18,960 --> 00:32:20,760
about what I can offer the other person.

853
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:23,120
Isn't that the wrong way to approach it?

854
00:32:24,120 --> 00:32:25,600
Then how do you think
I should approach it?

855
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:28,960
You should start

856
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:29,880
with your own feelings.

857
00:32:30,360 --> 00:32:30,780
Right?

858
00:32:30,780 --> 00:32:33,380
(You should start
with your own feelings)

